A||||18||Oreif||Village Pontiac Car Show. It was a nice day!||||6||
Z||000000||Oreif||06-24-2001||06:02 PM||||We had a nice day at the Village Pontiac All GM car show. Out of 14 classes of cars, Fiero's were the largest group (8 Fiero's and 1 Finale). Archie had the Finale with the different trunk lid. (Looks Great!) There were 4 V-8 cars there. Haze entered his 88 but not the 85. (The 85 is having the interior revamped) I wish I would have brought my camera. But Haze took some pic's. (Haze, I hope you got some good ones of Dave G's SE  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">   ) Saw some oher neat cars too!<BR>The only bad thing was on the way home I turned a corner and the plastic battery side cover/wall came loose and the power wire for the stereo touched the water pump pulley and cut into the power line for the stereo.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> (Always fuse your power lines!) The fuse blew so 1/2 the way home was just the rumble from the exhaust. Oh well gotta buy a fuse and repair the plastic side cover/wall. Going to have to brace it better. I think the weight of the fuseholder + the age of the plastic is my problem.<P>Still it was a good day.<BR><P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg">    <BR><B><I>Got Emblems?</I></B>||||reg||6
Z||000001||mrgone||06-24-2001||07:02 PM||||mine is held on by a bunjee cord, bolted under the suspention cap<BR>wasnt that a nice thing for the PO to do?<BR>no.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Bazooka||06-24-2001||07:16 PM||||Oreif,<BR>   It seemed to be a 'small' kind of show. Being all GM, It would have been nicer to see more Street Rods(only 4), Camaros(only 2), Corvettes (only 5), even newer Firebirds. No Malibus or Chevelles, just 2 Novas and quite a few non-collector cars (the big boats with 4 doors and lotsa weight). We did have a good representation of Fieros tho.  <BR>**************************************<BR>[QUOTE]Originally posted by Oreif:<BR>[B]We had a nice day at the Village Pontiac All GM car show. Out of 14 classes of cars, Fiero's were the largest group (8 Fiero's) There were 4 V-8 cars there. Haze entered his 88 but not the 85. (The 85 is having the interior revamped) I wish I would have brought my camera. But Haze took some pic's. (Haze, I hope you got some good ones of Dave G's SE   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">   ) Saw some oher neat cars too!<BR>Still it was a good day.<P>||||reg||1
